          "source_id": "vllm-vendor",
          "origin": "live",
          "text": "Dear vLLM Team,\r\n\r\nWe are a security research group, and while we are impressed with vLLM’s innovative design, particularly the efficiency of its PageAttention mechanism and chunk-based token management, we have identified a potential security vulnerability. This issue arises from the prefix caching mechanism, which may expose the system to a timing side-channel attack.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nWhen a new prompt is processed, if the PageAttention mechanism finds a matching prefix chunk, the prefill process speeds up, which is reflected in the TTFT (Time to First Token). Our tests revealed that the timing differences caused by matching chunks are significant enough to be recognized and exploited.\r\n",
          "title": "Potential Timing Side-Channel Vulnerability in vLLM’s Chunk-Based Prefix Caching",
